{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":19052385},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":19073508},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":19076118},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":19076541},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":19076940},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":19077062}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n# Step 1: Dataset Inspection & Integrity Check\n\nBefore training the YOLO object detection model, we first inspect the\ndataset structure and verify the quality of the image-label pairs.\n\nIn this step, we will:\n\n- Define dataset paths\n- Check the dataset directories\n- Count images and annotation files\n- Check image-label correspondence\n- Validate YOLO annotations\n- Analyze class distribution\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import os\nfrom glob import glob\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nDATASET_DIR = \"/kaggle/input/datasets/alinaliaquat/surgical-tools\"\n\nTRAIN_IMG_DIR = os.path.join(DATASET_DIR, \"train\", \"images\")\nTRAIN_LABEL_DIR = os.path.join(DATASET_DIR, \"train\", \"labels\")\n\nVAL_IMG_DIR = os.path.join(DATASET_DIR, \"valid\", \"images\")\nVAL_LABEL_DIR = os.path.join(DATASET_DIR, \"valid\", \"labels\")\n\nTEST_IMG_DIR = os.path.join(DATASET_DIR, \"test\", \"images\")\nTEST_LABEL_DIR = os.path.join(DATASET_DIR, \"test\", \"labels\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.89598Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.896478Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.904427Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.896451Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.903546Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":1},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Checking Dataset Structure\n\nBefore processing the dataset, we verify that all required directories\nexist at the expected locations. This helps detect incorrect paths or missing dataset folders before\nrunning further analysis.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"directories = {\n    \"Train Images\": TRAIN_IMG_DIR,\n    \"Train Labels\": TRAIN_LABEL_DIR,\n    \"Validation Images\": VAL_IMG_DIR,\n    \"Validation Labels\": VAL_LABEL_DIR,\n    \"Test Images\": TEST_IMG_DIR,\n    \"Test Labels\": TEST_LABEL_DIR\n}\n\nfor name, path in directories.items():\n    print(f\"{name:25} : {os.path.exists(path)}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.906546Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.906894Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.931569Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.906873Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:02.931014Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Train Images              : True\nTrain Labels              : True\nValidation Images         : True\nValidation Labels         : True\nTest Images               : True\nTest Labels               : True\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Image and Label Count\n\nCount the images and corresponding YOLO annotation files in the\ntraining, validation, and test sets.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"IMAGE_EXTENSIONS = [\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".bmp\", \".webp\"]\n\n\ndef get_image_files(directory):\n    files = []\n\n    for extension in IMAGE_EXTENSIONS:\n        files.extend(glob(os.path.join(directory, f\"*{extension}\")))\n\n    return sorted(files)\n\n\ndef get_label_files(directory):\n    return sorted(glob(os.path.join(directory, \"*.txt\")))\n\n\ntrain_images = get_image_files(TRAIN_IMG_DIR)\ntrain_labels = get_label_files(TRAIN_LABEL_DIR)\n\nval_images = get_image_files(VAL_IMG_DIR)\nval_labels = get_label_files(VAL_LABEL_DIR)\n\ntest_images = get_image_files(TEST_IMG_DIR)\ntest_labels = get_label_files(TEST_LABEL_DIR)\n\n\nprint(\"TRAIN\")\nprint(f\"Images : {len(train_images)}\")\nprint(f\"Labels : {len(train_labels)}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nVALIDATION\")\nprint(f\"Images : {len(val_images)}\")\nprint(f\"Labels : {len(val_labels)}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nTEST\")\nprint(f\"Images : {len(test_images)}\")\nprint(f\"Labels : {len(test_labels)}\")\n\nprint(\n    f\"\\nTotal Images: \"\n    f\"{len(train_images) + len(val_images) + len(test_images)}\"\n)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.63198Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.632258Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.980461Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.632235Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.978258Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"TRAIN\nImages : 5250\nLabels : 5250\n\nVALIDATION\nImages : 1476\nLabels : 1476\n\nTEST\nImages : 724\nLabels : 724\n\nTotal Images: 7450\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Image–Label Correspondence\n\nVerify that every image has a corresponding YOLO annotation file\nand that there are no annotation files without their corresponding images","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def get_base_names(files):\n    return {\n        os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(file))[0]\n        for file in files\n    }\n\n\ndef check_image_label_pairs(image_files, label_files):\n    image_names = get_base_names(image_files)\n    label_names = get_base_names(label_files)\n\n    missing_labels = image_names - label_names\n    orphan_labels = label_names - image_names\n\n    return missing_labels, orphan_labels\n\n\nsplits = {\n    \"Train\": (train_images, train_labels),\n    \"Validation\": (val_images, val_labels),\n    \"Test\": (test_images, test_labels)\n}\n\n\nfor split_name, (images, labels) in splits.items():\n\n    missing, orphan = check_image_label_pairs(images, labels)\n\n    print(f\"\\n{split_name}\")\n    print(\"-\" * 40)\n    print(f\"Missing labels : {len(missing)}\")\n    print(f\"Orphan labels  : {len(orphan)}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.98169Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.981966Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.038877Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:03.981937Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.038084Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"\nTrain\n----------------------------------------\nMissing labels : 0\nOrphan labels  : 0\n\nValidation\n----------------------------------------\nMissing labels : 0\nOrphan labels  : 0\n\nTest\n----------------------------------------\nMissing labels : 0\nOrphan labels  : 0\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Class Definition\n\nDefine the 12 surgical-tool classes specified in `data.yaml`\nand map each class ID to its corresponding class name","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"CLASS_NAMES = [\n    \"7 Metzenbaum Scissors\",\n    \"9 Metzenbaum Scissors\",\n    \"Allis Tissue Forceps\",\n    \"Babcock Tissue Forceps\",\n    \"Crile Artery Forceps\",\n    \"Curved Mayo Scissor\",\n    \"Lahey Forceps\",\n    \"Mayo Needle Holder\",\n    \"Scalpel\",\n    \"Sponge Forceps\",\n    \"Straight Dissection Clamp\",\n    \"Straight Mayo Scissor\"\n]\n\nNUM_CLASSES = len(CLASS_NAMES)\n\nfor class_id, class_name in enumerate(CLASS_NAMES):\n    print(f\"{class_id}: {class_name}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.832873Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.833704Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.839569Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.833656Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.838904Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"0: 7 Metzenbaum Scissors\n1: 9 Metzenbaum Scissors\n2: Allis Tissue Forceps\n3: Babcock Tissue Forceps\n4: Crile Artery Forceps\n5: Curved Mayo Scissor\n6: Lahey Forceps\n7: Mayo Needle Holder\n8: Scalpel\n9: Sponge Forceps\n10: Straight Dissection Clamp\n11: Straight Mayo Scissor\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Data Cleaning & Annotation Validation\n\nValidate the YOLO annotations before performing exploratory data analysis.\n\nEach annotation must follow:\n\nclass_id x_center y_center width height\n\nWe will check:\n\n- Annotation format\n- Valid class IDs\n- Normalized coordinates\n- Positive bounding-box dimensions","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def validate_labels(label_dir):\n\n    errors = []\n\n    for label_file in get_label_files(label_dir):\n\n        with open(label_file, \"r\") as file:\n\n            for line_number, line in enumerate(file, start=1):\n\n                values = line.strip().split()\n\n                if len(values) != 5:\n                    errors.append((label_file, line_number, \"Invalid format\"))\n                    continue\n\n                try:\n                    class_id = int(values[0])\n                    x, y, width, height = map(float, values[1:])\n                except ValueError:\n                    errors.append((label_file, line_number, \"Non-numeric value\"))\n                    continue\n\n                if not 0 <= class_id < NUM_CLASSES:\n                    errors.append((label_file, line_number, \"Invalid class ID\"))\n\n                if not all(0 <= value <= 1 for value in [x, y, width, height]):\n                    errors.append((label_file, line_number, \"Coordinate outside 0-1\"))\n\n                if width <= 0 or height <= 0:\n                    errors.append((label_file, line_number, \"Invalid box dimensions\"))\n\n    return errors\n\n\nfor split_name, label_dir in [\n    (\"Train\", TRAIN_LABEL_DIR),\n    (\"Validation\", VAL_LABEL_DIR),\n    (\"Test\", TEST_LABEL_DIR)\n]:\n\n    errors = validate_labels(label_dir)\n\n    print(f\"{split_name}: {len(errors)} invalid annotations\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.843045Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.843523Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:24.427559Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:04.843493Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:24.426717Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Train: 0 invalid annotations\nValidation: 0 invalid annotations\nTest: 0 invalid annotations\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":6},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n\nAfter verifying the dataset structure and annotation integrity,\nwe now explore the distribution and characteristics of the\nobject-detection dataset.\n\nWe will analyze:\n\n- Class distribution\n- Number of objects per image\n- Bounding-box width and height\n- Bounding-box area\n- Object locations\n- Small vs. large objects\n- Sample images with bounding boxes\n\nThe goal is to understand the dataset before preprocessing,\naugmentation, and model training","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3.1 Class Distribution\n\nWe first analyze the distribution of object instances across the\n12 surgical-tool classes.\n\nThis helps identify class imbalance and understand which surgical\ntools are more or less represented in the training dataset","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n\ndef get_class_distribution(label_dir):\n\n    class_counts = Counter()\n\n    for label_file in get_label_files(label_dir):\n\n        with open(label_file, \"r\") as file:\n\n            for line in file:\n\n                values = line.strip().split()\n\n                if len(values) == 5:\n                    class_id = int(values[0])\n                    class_counts[class_id] += 1\n\n    return class_counts\n\n\n# Calculate training class distribution\ntrain_distribution = get_class_distribution(\n    TRAIN_LABEL_DIR\n)\n\n\n# Get count for every class\nclass_counts = [\n    train_distribution[class_id]\n    for class_id in range(NUM_CLASSES)\n]\n\n\n# Display counts\nfor class_id, count in enumerate(class_counts):\n    print(f\"{CLASS_NAMES[class_id]:30} : {count}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:24.428912Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:24.42924Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.049947Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:24.429217Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.049324Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"7 Metzenbaum Scissors          : 524\n9 Metzenbaum Scissors          : 560\nAllis Tissue Forceps           : 316\nBabcock Tissue Forceps         : 365\nCrile Artery Forceps           : 313\nCurved Mayo Scissor            : 789\nLahey Forceps                  : 324\nMayo Needle Holder             : 485\nScalpel                        : 713\nSponge Forceps                 : 346\nStraight Dissection Clamp      : 758\nStraight Mayo Scissor          : 667\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n\nplt.bar(CLASS_NAMES, class_counts)\n\nplt.title(\"Training Set: Surgical Tool Class Distribution\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Surgical Tool\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Number of Object Instances\")\n\nplt.xticks(\n    rotation=75,\n    ha=\"right\"\n)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.050759Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.051046Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.316988Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.051024Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.316181Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":8},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Number of Objects per Image\n\nAn object-detection image can contain one or multiple objects.\n\nWe calculate how many annotated surgical tools are present in\neach training image.\n\nThis helps us understand the object density of the dataset.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"objects_per_image = []\n\n\nfor label_file in train_labels:\n\n    with open(label_file, \"r\") as file:\n\n        annotations = [\n            line.strip()\n            for line in file\n            if line.strip()\n        ]\n\n    objects_per_image.append(\n        len(annotations)\n    )\n\n\nprint(f\"Total images: {len(objects_per_image)}\")\nprint(\n    f\"Average objects per image: \"\n    f\"{sum(objects_per_image) / len(objects_per_image):.2f}\"\n)\nprint(\n    f\"Minimum objects per image: \"\n    f\"{min(objects_per_image)}\"\n)\nprint(\n    f\"Maximum objects per image: \"\n    f\"{max(objects_per_image)}\"\n)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.318473Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.319101Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.800947Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:27.319079Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.800104Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Total images: 5250\nAverage objects per image: 1.17\nMinimum objects per image: 1\nMaximum objects per image: 4\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":9},{"cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n\nplt.hist(\n    objects_per_image,\n    bins=range(\n        min(objects_per_image),\n        max(objects_per_image) + 2\n    ),\n    edgecolor=\"black\"\n)\n\nplt.title(\"Number of Objects per Training Image\")\nplt.xlabel(\"Number of Objects\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Number of Images\")\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.80188Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.802142Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.955307Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.802122Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.954704Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":10},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Bounding Box Width and Height\n\nYOLO stores bounding boxes using normalized coordinates:\n\n    class_id x_center y_center width height\n\nThe width and height values range from 0 to 1.\n\nWe analyze their distributions to understand the size of the\nsurgical tools relative to the image dimensions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"bbox_widths = []\nbbox_heights = []\n\n\nfor label_file in train_labels:\n\n    with open(label_file, \"r\") as file:\n\n        for line in file:\n\n            values = line.strip().split()\n\n            if len(values) == 5:\n\n                _, _, _, width, height = map(\n                    float,\n                    values\n                )\n\n                bbox_widths.append(width)\n                bbox_heights.append(height)\n\n\nprint(f\"Total bounding boxes: {len(bbox_widths)}\")\n\nprint(\n    f\"Average width : \"\n    f\"{sum(bbox_widths) / len(bbox_widths):.3f}\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    f\"Average height: \"\n    f\"{sum(bbox_heights) / len(bbox_heights):.3f}\"\n)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.956118Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.956362Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-20T16:53:32.518295Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-20T16:53:29.95634Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-20T16:53:32.517699Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Total bounding boxes: 6160\nAverage width : 0.400\nAverage height: 0.525\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":11},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Data Preprocessing & Augme